{%- comment -%}
  Display name for a product.

  Half the catalogue is titled cleanly — "The Borrowdale Bolster Bed" — and
  half carries a search tail: "The Braithwaite Orthopaedic Dog Bed — Senior,
  Low Front, 122 × 89 × 17cm". Both are right for Google. Side by side in a
  four-up grid they read as two different shops, and that split is most of
  what makes a catalogue look assembled rather than made.

  This trims the tail for display only. The product's own title is never
  touched, so the search result, the structured data, the browser tab and the
  order confirmation all keep every keyword they were written for.

  What counts as a tail
    Only a spaced em dash or en dash. A hyphen does not, because plenty of
    real names carry one, and a comma does not, because "The Kendal Bed, Grey"
    is a name and not a tail.

  What is refused
    A separator with nothing in front of it, and a head so short it is clearly
    not the name — better a long title than a card labelled "The".

  Required
    product   a product object, or `title` as a plain string

  Optional
    title     trim this string instead of the product's title
    full      true renders the title untouched, for anywhere the keywords
              are the point
    fallback  used when the resolved title is empty
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign t = title | default: product.title | default: fallback | default: '' | strip

  assign out = t
  unless full
    comment
      Em dash first, then en dash, so a title carrying both loses only the
      longest tail rather than being cut twice at the wrong place.
    endcomment
    assign marks = '—|–' | split: '|'
    for mark in marks
      assign sep = ' ' | append: mark | append: ' '
      assign parts = out | split: sep
      if parts.size > 1
        assign head = parts.first | strip
        assign head_len = head | size
        if head_len >= 6
          assign out = head
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endunless

  comment
    A trailing comma or colon is left over often enough to be worth removing:
    "The Wasdale Bolster Bed," reads as a mistake, not a name.
  endcomment
  assign last = out | slice: -1
  if last == ',' or last == ':' or last == '·'
    assign keep = out | size | minus: 1
    assign out = out | slice: 0, keep | strip
  endif
-%}
{{- out -}}
